("Default switch", "With storage=None, the environment selects dense/packed if set; otherwise the shipped choice is packed. Eligible CUDA fp32 4-bit D64/D128 K becomes PackedSpKeys, packed_prepare/append creates TQ4 codes and norms, and attention uses spq1 rotate/bulk (bulk_shared at G4/8), spo2/spo4 ordered selection, and spo2 merge under the packed table. Two-bit or missing-backend defaults fall back to dense with a reason; explicit ineligible packed raises. Dense opt-out keeps the dense quantizer and native epsilon/split-K path/table. The dense wrapper body is byte-identical (574 bytes). Old four-bit callers now receive an owned object, need packed margins, get a prefill refusal, and raw dense entries reject that object. Diagnostics still return output/mask. Identity/generation/revision and bounded append checks work under the documented unchanged-prefix contract, but the factory cannot reserve growth (F09), native capacity can narrow (F04), and the table pin is bypassable at use (F01). On identical bulk scores, margins and partition width, no default packed selection rule skips a key selected by dense: both use inclusive prefix max and >=. L=1 causal exposes all S keys; sinks do not enter selection. Read apa_sp2.py:61-136, apa_packed.py:88-146,215-437, packed_launcher.cuh:14-55, launcher.cuh:169-245, parallel.cuh:90-106 and apa_sp1_1.cuh:56-73; ran receipts 016,036,039,045."),
