("Determinism and numerics", "Source reasoning supports bitwise repeatability for valid, unchanged inputs on one device under the default-stream contract: output writes are disjoint; integer tickets select the last CTA but do not set summation order; merges visit chunks in fixed ascending order; no floating-point atomics are used. This CPU-only review did not measure run-to-run GPU output. I independently inventoried 6,922 retained B/F LF1 arrays and, after excluding one combined timing/byte-census structure, rechecked 6,921 using dtype/shape checks, informative same-width unsigned views, and np.array_equal: all equal. That is finite-case evidence, not universal determinism. The receipt uses one build per side and the engine's default logical CUDA device; it does not record a physical GPU UUID/model, so that identity cannot be independently reconstructed. For finite nonnegative denominators, >0 and !=0 give identical results, including +/-0 behavior; finite operands alone can overflow and change B's finite zero into F's NaN (F06). Read merge.cuh:14-30 and EB3/4 fused merge chains/tickets; ran 023,028,035,037,039,041. No model-quality or hardware-portability claim follows."),
("Tests and evidence", "Both requested CPU suites pass: 40 policy IDs and 15 F1 IDs (55 total), recomputed from the verbose log. They cover policy/forwarding, identity, loader and macro checks, mainly with fakes. Existing GPU receipts cover registered finite identity, 32 vector-refusal IDs plus six controls, 63 refusal/knob checks and 11 FH timeout/knob checks. I recomputed 6,921 array identities from 6,922 retained arrays (one timing structure excluded), 44 regression files/2,078 IDs and 729 CPU regression IDs; outcomes match their before arms, including 36 GPU failures/15 errors and 125 CPU failures/15 errors, not an all-green suite. LF2 remains FAIL: 246/260 checks true, including two failed L19 controls and 12 Inf predictions; supplementary LF2S has 17/26 true and is PASS only because its nine Inf misses are predictions. Missing coverage includes pin bypass, reserved factory growth and large capacities, raw empty helpers, EB3 timeline at G3/5/6/7/8, -Inf and V Inf, all -Inf logits, finite overflow/non-finite sinks, and column-level non-finite behavior. These lines do not re-establish ticket growth, multiple devices, alternate streams or repeatability; no physical-device UUID is recorded. Read both entire CPU test files and scripts/apa_p1f1_gpu.py LF1-LF6; ran 021-022,025,029-032,035-037,041,043. Full gap matrix and all exit/log hashes follow."),
